		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4330&amp;p=32538#p32538"><![CDATA[
I have a TYT 9600 setup in hotspot mode on a high gain antenna (11.9db). This works great, people from all over the Phoenix Az area can join in on Brandmeister or TGIF. My concern is FCC station ID compliance. Yaesu and D-Star as far as I know embed the station operators call sign in the digital header. With DMR its the DMR ID that's in the header and that's not a government issued ID. My thought was to set my call sign as the talker alias but I have not been able to verify if that would meet compliance or not. Any feedback would be much appreciated.<br><br>BTW thanks for the amazing work on this firmware, it took the TYT9600 and UV390 from radios I'd probably just give away to the best radios I've ever owned.<br><br>73's<br><br>KD7YCX<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6352">KD7YCX</a> — Sat Aug 17, 2024 11:39 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
